---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="Privacy approach for the SPARK Community Hub.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Community trust" title="Privacy by separation and restraint." description="The public website is designed to publish community information—not to become a database of applications, travel, mentoring, or sensitive participant records." status="preview" statusLabel="Initial policy" compact />
  <section class="section section-white"><article class="narrow prose"><h2>Public website</h2><p>This is a statically generated public website. Content committed to its public GitHub repository should be treated as public and durable. The site does not currently provide user accounts, private profiles, comments, or an internal participant directory.</p><h2>Information we intentionally do not collect here</h2><ul><li>Forum applications or selection records.</li><li>Mentorship preferences or identity and affinity information.</li><li>Flight, lodging, passport, reimbursement, or family details.</li><li>Dietary, disability, medical, or accessibility information.</li><li>Private attendee contact lists or project data.</li></ul><p>Forum applications are submitted through Google Forms, outside this website. Google may ask you to sign in. Refer to the application form for the information requested. Other participant workflows will be handled separately as they become available. Application responses and sensitive participant information are not stored on this public website or in its GitHub repository.</p><h2>Email</h2><p>When you email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>, your message is processed by the relevant email provider and institution. Send only the information necessary for your inquiry. Do not email sensitive information requested for future forms.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Links may take you to external application forms, event registration, code repositories, videos, or resources. Those services control their own privacy practices. External destinations will be identified where practical.</p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>The initial website does not intentionally install advertising trackers or custom analytics. Hosting infrastructure may retain operational logs under its own policies. If privacy-aware analytics are added later, this page will identify the provider, purpose, data collected, and available controls.</p><h2>Questions and corrections</h2><p>To request a correction or removal of public content involving you, contact the organizing team. Some records may also remain in Git history or third-party caches, so the team will explain what can reasonably be changed.</p><p><em>Last updated: November 9, 2026.</em></p></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
